<h2>Siri AI Requirements</h2><br/>
On the &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj; and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-tv/">Apple TV</a> 4K models that support &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI, the home owner in the Home app must have an Apple Intelligence-enabled iPhone or <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad/">iPad</a> on the latest version of the software. &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI has to be turned on, and it has to be set to a supported language. Other members of the household don't need an Apple Intelligence-enabled device once &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI is turned on, except for personal requests.<br/>
<br/>
HomeView does not require an Apple Intelligence-enabled iPhone or &zwnj;iPad&zwnj; for &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI, except for requests that use personal context.<br/>
<br/>
&zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI for HomeView, &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; 4K, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/homepod-mini/">HomePod mini 2</a> is English only and is limited to the United States, Australia, Canada, India, New Zealand, Singapore, South Africa, and the UK at launch.<br/>
<h2>EU Restrictions</h2><br/>
&zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI is not available in the EU on the iPhone and &zwnj;iPad&zwnj;, so &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI won't be available for home devices that support it. HomeView isn't even launching in the EU.<br/>
